          "id": "c14-l2-e6",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This loop prints one value too many (garbage after the 3). Which line is wrong?",
          "code": [
            "#include <stdio.h>",
            "",
            "int main() {",
            "    int a[3] = {1, 2, 3};",
            "    int *p = a;",
            "    while (p <= a + 3) {",
            "        printf(\"%d\\n\", *p);",
            "        p++;",
            "    }",
            "    return 0;",
            "}"
          ],
          "answer": 5,
          "explanation": "a + 3 is one past the end. The loop must stop when p < a + 3 is false."
